# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenAI credentials — supports BOTH a personal OpenAI key and the EY Azure key.
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in.  The backend loads it automatically.
#
# Selection rule: if OPENAI_ENDPOINT is set → Azure/EY mode; otherwise normal
# OpenAI (api.openai.com).  Both modes read OPENAI_API_KEY.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Required (either provider)
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Home / personal OpenAI: leave everything below BLANK ──────────────────────

# ── Work / EY Azure OpenAI: set these ─────────────────────────────────────────
# OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://eyq-incubator.europe.fabric.ey.com/eyq/eu/api
# OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-02-15-preview
# OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o                 # Azure DEPLOYMENT name for QA + judge
# OPENAI_EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-large # Azure DEPLOYMENT name for embeddings
#                                           # (omit to use a local embedding backend)

# ── Corporate proxy (EY Zscaler) TLS — set ONE if HTTPS calls fail to verify ──
# ZSCALER_CERT=C:\path\to\ZscalerRootCertificate-2048-SHA256.pem
# OPENAI_CA_BUNDLE=C:\path\to\combined_bundle.pem
